## Local development

Install the shared developer tools from the registered `openstudio-si` PyPI package:

```bash
python -m pip install "openstudio-si[plugin-dev]"
openstudio-si plugin check-project .
openstudio-si plugin validate ./plugin
mkdir -p dist
openstudio-si plugin export ./plugin --output ./dist/plugin > dist/export-report.json
openstudio-si plugin check-hosts dist/export-report.json
```

Use a release that includes these commands; older releases do not provide the
extra. The installation includes the OpenStudio SDK and runtime dependencies.
No separate tooling download or lab-managed tooling lock is required. Native
host checks also require Claude Code and Codex. CI maintains their versions
centrally and installs them with npm --ignore-scripts.

